WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.820
Welcome to Monitor and Control. In this lesson, we explore this purpose: Compare actual results against a plan and act on significant deviations.

2
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:20.460
Consider this scenario. A project slips three weeks with no escalation. First understand the problem before producing documentation.

3
00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:30.990
Start with two steps: Define control points and tolerances. Then Observe actual performance. Each step should be explained and evidenced.

4
00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:40.820
Continue with Investigate significant variance. Then Adjust actions and reforecast. Verify the results against the intended outcome.

5
00:00:40.820 --> 00:01:00.410
Stronger evidence looks like this: Stronger: contemporaneous variance reports, milestones, issue escalations tied to real work. Weaker evidence would be: Weaker: collecting status without responding to variance; no trace of consistent use. Triangulate independent sources.

6
00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:14.660
Now your turn. Review four documents and two interviews, identify inconsistencies and complete the mastery challenge. This video is an independent teaching explanation, not official CMMI model wording.
